  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 518.17 Personnel",
  "priorExpiration": "2012-03-15",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 518.17 Personnel.\n\n(a) Each municipal agent shall notify the department in writing of all employees who will be engaged in the process of registering vehicles. The department shall also be notified in writing of the termination, resignation, or retirement of the municipal agent or any employee.\n\n(b) The notification required by this section shall initially be given with the application required by Saf-C 518.02.\n\n(c) Each municipal agent shall notify the department of all changes affecting any personnel notification previously filed.\n\n(d) In the event a new city or town clerk is elected who has not yet been appointed as a municipal agent, other employees who are certified to register vehicles in that city or town shall be allowed to continue uninterrupted as a municipal agent, until the new city or town clerk is appointed as a municipal agent.\n\nSource. #7972, eff 10-17-03 (See Revision Note #1 at chapter heading for Saf-C 500); ss by #9995, INTERIM, eff 9-17-11, EXPIRED: 3-15-12\n\nNew. #10135, eff 5-23-12; ss by #13521, eff 1-13-23 (formerly Saf-C 519.17)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c500.html"
